# 📊 HR Analytics Dashboard — Power BI

## 📌 Project Overview

This project presents an interactive **HR Analytics Dashboard** developed using **Microsoft Power BI**.

The dashboard transforms HR data into meaningful insights by analyzing employee demographics, workforce distribution, attrition, departments, job roles, and key HR performance indicators.

The project demonstrates practical skills in **data cleaning, data transformation, data modeling, DAX, KPI development, and data visualization**.

---

## 🎯 Project Objectives

The main objectives of this project are to:

- Analyze employee demographics and workforce composition
- Monitor key HR performance indicators
- Analyze employee attrition and identify trends
- Compare departments and job roles
- Build interactive and dynamic HR reports
- Create meaningful KPIs using DAX
- Support data-driven HR decision-making

---

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies

| Tool / Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Power BI** | Dashboard development and data visualization |
| **DAX** | Measures, KPIs, and analytical calculations |
| **Power Query** | Data cleaning and transformation |
| **Data Modeling** | Building relationships between tables |
| **Data Visualization** | Interactive charts, KPIs, and reports |

---

## 📊 Dashboard Preview

### HR Analytics Dashboard

![HR Analytics Dashboard](Screenshots/dashboard.png)

The dashboard provides an interactive overview of the organization's workforce and HR-related KPIs.

Users can interact with the report using filters and slicers to explore different employee segments, departments, roles, and other dimensions.

---

## 🔎 Key Areas of Analysis

The dashboard focuses on several important HR metrics and business questions:

### 👥 Employee Analysis

- Total number of employees
- Employee demographics
- Workforce distribution
- Department distribution
- Job-role analysis

### 📉 Attrition Analysis

- Employee attrition
- Attrition rate
- Attrition by department
- Attrition by job role
- Identification of workforce trends

### 📈 KPI Analysis

The dashboard includes dynamic KPIs designed to provide a quick overview of workforce performance and HR metrics.

---

## 🧹 Data Cleaning & Transformation

**Power Query** was used to prepare the dataset before analysis.

The data preparation process included:

- Handling missing values
- Removing duplicate records
- Correcting data types
- Cleaning and standardizing data
- Transforming columns
- Creating fields required for analysis
- Preparing the dataset for the Power BI data model

---

## 🧩 Data Modeling

A structured data model was created in Power BI to support interactive analysis and ensure that the dashboard calculations work correctly.

![Data Model](Documentation/data_model.png)

The model includes relationships between the relevant data tables and was designed to support efficient filtering, aggregation, and analysis.

---

## 🧮 DAX & KPI Development

**DAX (Data Analysis Expressions)** was used to create calculated measures and dynamic KPIs throughout the dashboard.

Examples of the types of calculations used include:

- Total Employees
- Employees Who Left
- Attrition Rate
- Employee Distribution
- Department-level metrics
- Percentage calculations
- Other HR analytical measures
